  "note": "CORRECTION. The approved review layout was media-with-text \u2014 one big image left, one big quote right, Tatcha's arrangement. Asked for a six-review slider, I replaced that layout with a six-across multi-column row of small tiles. That was wrong: the layout was already right and only needed sliding added. This restores media-with-text and gives it six blocks, one per product.\n\nThe slide behaviour is CSS in the site-wide block: .media-with-text is `display:grid; overflow:hidden` with one __item per block, so overriding it to `auto-flow 100%` with overflow-x auto and scroll snap makes the six items advance one at a time \u2014 Tatcha's behaviour, no theme file touched.\n\nImages are v2, regenerated after Malcolm's note: casting varied across ethnicities to match Tatcha's set, and crops tightened so the face fills the frame with the top of the head cut off, where v1 framed whole heads with air around them.\n\nCOPY IS STILL PLACEHOLDER \u2014 six invented names and quotes on a store with no orders.\n\nCaught before it shipped: the plan had inherited uploaded_handle values from the v1 upload, so the live page would have kept showing the v1 images even though the local files were regenerated. Handles cleared and the v2 files uploaded under -v2 filenames, since v1 already occupies the originals in Files and Shopify would have suffixed a same-name upload.",
